<div class="card">
    <h2>Step 2: Code of Conduct Notice</h2>
    <p class="form-hint">
        All medical-service providers, employed staff, contractors, eligible family
        members, and re-employed annuitants are expected to uphold the following
        principles.
    </p>

    <div class="principles-prose">
        <p class="preamble">
            This Code of Conduct reflects four fundamental principles:
            (1)&nbsp;responsibilities to patients; (2)&nbsp;respect for patients and
            colleagues; (3)&nbsp;adherence to established medical standards;
            (4)&nbsp;acknowledgement that medicine is an ever-evolving field that requires
            providers to stay current in their fields to ensure excellent patient care.
        </p>

        <ol class="principles-list">
            <li>Ensure all individuals eligible for the medical programme can access timely care.</li>
            <li>Provide health care with competence and compassion.</li>
            <li>Treat patients and colleagues with dignity and respect.</li>
            <li>Ensure every encounter is conducted without discrimination based on age, sexual orientation, gender, race, ethnicity, national origin, language, disease, disability, or religion.</li>
            <li>Do not engage in retaliation against colleagues or patients for any reason.</li>
            <li>Make all reasonable attempts to respectfully provide care to each patient. If for any reason a provider is unable to do so, ensure the patient receives non-judgemental and prompt referral to another clinician, or seek alternative options to preserve patient autonomy.</li>
            <li>Provide each patient with the information needed for considered decision-making about their health. A patient&rsquo;s informed and voluntary consent must be secured, when possible, before initiating a medical procedure.</li>
            <li>Safeguard patient confidentiality, medical information, and privacy.</li>
            <li>Report unintended events promptly, honestly, and thoroughly through appropriate channels.</li>
            <li>Commit to continued education and adaptation: fulfil educational and training requirements, seek out and apply the soundest medical guidance, and, in situations of uncertainty, ask for help.</li>
            <li>Follow guidelines and policies with professionalism, honesty, and integrity.</li>
            <li>Report wrongdoing (including violations of this Code of Conduct) to the appropriate authorities.</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="closing-note">
            Please read each principle carefully before proceeding to acknowledge and sign.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
